Fixed. `src/config.js` dereferenced `config.server.port` unguarded, so a missing `server` section threw instead of falling back, and an empty `server` section returned `undefined`.

```js
export function getPort(config) {
  return config.server?.port ?? 3000;
}
```

Optional chaining handles the missing `server`, and `??` covers the missing `port` (keeping `0` a valid port, unlike `||`). All 3 tests pass; nothing under `test/` was touched.

